# What this file holds for the owner. There is no catch-all: a path listed here
# is one whose change can do harm that no later check would catch, and every
# other path merges on a signed commit, green checks and the reviewer App's
# approval. GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so a line with no owner
# releases what an earlier line took.
#
# scripts/test_codeowners.py holds a fixed table of sample paths for every class
# below and fails when one of them changes owner.

# The rules themselves, and the owner's own instructions.
CLAUDE.md                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/AUTHORISATIONS.md       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.claude/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tools/floors.tsv        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The scripts the plan and deploy jobs run with secrets in scope, and the tests
# that gate them. That includes the committed-secret guard and its test (a
# required check that plan and deploy need) and test_generate_tenant_repo.py
# (it runs in both required checks), and the generator (see below). Only the
# documents beside them are released, below.
/scripts/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The test of the test:render gate, which runs in the required Type check.
/test/                   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# What decides the program Pulumi runs, and what runs while it is installed,
# in the jobs that hold the state credentials, the passphrase and the deploy key.
# package.json: `main` picks the program, lifecycle hooks run on install.
# pnpm-workspace.yaml: the list of install scripts allowed to run.
# tsconfig.json: its ts-node block runs code inside the Pulumi process.
# .pnpmfile.cjs and .pnpmfile.mjs: pnpm loads them on its own at install time,
# so a file added later would run in the jobs that hold secrets.
# known_hosts: what the deploy job's SSH trusts.
/package.json            @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/pnpm-workspace.yaml     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.npmrc                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.pnpmfile.cjs           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.pnpmfile.mjs           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/known_hosts             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/Pulumi.yaml             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/Pulumi.*.yaml           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/index.ts                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/config.ts               @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/tsconfig.json           @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The owner's words: licence text.
/LICENSE                 @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The generator stays owned: the platform's provision-tenant workflow runs it in
# a job that holds the tenant state keys and the provisioning App key, and it
# writes the secret-bearing CI workflow into every new tenant repository.
/scripts/generate-tenant-repo.py @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Released from /scripts/ above: the documents beside the scripts.
/scripts/*.md

# SYNC-1 suffix: shared with every repo, and these must stay the final lines
# (GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so anything after or between them
# can silently take ownership). A repo adds its own patterns above, never here.
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
